    "editorial:Flashcards_en.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "e51e6bdb49d0591d280f72a7a94936458ff2080fcbd1bcad1d5890902a75eae5",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- Card 1 back states a general rule \"When positions from opposite ends are given with no overlap, total = (position from left) + (position from right).\" This is incorrect; the correct general rule for no overlap is total = (position from left) + (position from right) + (number of people between them). The given rule only applies when there are zero people between them. → The general rule should include the people between: total = left position + right position + people between (for non-overlap cases).",
        "- Card 10 answer claims only B or E can be at the extreme right, but C can also be at the extreme right if A and C occupy the last two positions (D at leftmost, A at 4th, C at 5th). → The extreme right can be B, C, or E; the answer should list all three possibilities."
      ],
